n":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":345,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:15:08Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-05T23:52:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T23:53:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123237","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123237","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123237.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123237.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThe pattern `unsigned_variable &= ~(1 << SOME_LAYER);` is present in many places in the codebase, especially anywhere with layers. This bit-shifts a signed integer, then flips the bits, which turns it into a negative number. Then, the bitwise-and with an unsigned variable causes a sanitizer error:\r\n\r\n> scene/3d/camera_3d.cpp:840:11: runtime error: implicit conversion from type 'int' of value -17 (32-bit, signed) to type 'unsigned int' changed the value to 4294967279 (32-bit, unsigned)\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes the issue by using an unsigned literal (`1u`) for the bit-shift, in cases where the destination of the computation is an unsigned variable. These were found with a search for `&= ~(1 <<`, I am not guaranteeing that I found every case of bit-shifts that should be unsigned, but at least these are a bunch that would previously be undefined behavior that are now fixed, plus the corresponding `|= 1 <<` and getters updated to match.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI used AI by copy-pasting Godot sanitizer errors to it and telling it to fix them. Then, I am investigating each manually, and submitting PRs when I am confident of the fix. For this one, I had the AI search for `&= ~(1 <<` and filter down the list, then I applied all of the changes manually - so the AI's role in this PR was purely exclusionary, filtering out places that I should not change because the destination is actually signed or because undefined behavior will never occur.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123237/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}